  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this dashboard is",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 6
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Customer X example: only customer-consumable Orka metrics\nBuilt to show what a customer's **own Prometheus + Grafana** can chart against the Customer X \"service review\" (Sept 2026) asks **R1, R2, D3 and O3**, using only endpoints documented as customer-scrapable.\n\n| Job in this stack | Endpoint scraped | Provides |\n|---|---|---|\n| `orka-operator` | `<orka LB IP>:8080/metrics` | the 10 `orka_operator_*` VM metrics |\n| `orka-nodes` | `<node IP>:9100/metrics` | node_exporter: filesystem, CPU, memory, load, network |\n| `kube-state-metrics` | `<orka LB IP>:9101/metrics` (here via a read-only port-forward) | node conditions, pod phases, node capacity |\n\nPanels whose title ends **(not available)** or the final text panel mark asks that **no endpoint documented as customer-reachable can answer**. Every panel's description (hover the **i** icon) lists its exact metric, job, labels and PromQL. Lab source: L20 (ORKL10000020). Full write-up: `docs/customer-x-example-dashboard.md`."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "R1 / O3 — Node health  (kube-state-metrics :9101, node_exporter :9100)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Nodes Ready",
      "description": "Metric: `kube_node_status_condition` (gauge, 0/1) from job `kube-state-metrics`.\nLabels used: `condition=\"Ready\"`, `status=\"true\"`.\nPromQL: count of series equal to 1.\nMeaning: Kubernetes' own view of how many nodes (masters included) report Ready. This is the closest customer-visible signal to ask R1 (node failure detection).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "count(kube_node_status_condition{condition=\"Ready\",status=\"true\"} == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Ready",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Nodes NotReady / Unknown",
      "description": "Metric: `kube_node_status_condition`, job `kube-state-metrics`.\nLabels: `condition=\"Ready\"`, `status=~\"false|unknown\"`.\nPromQL: count of those series equal to 1, `or vector(0)` so the panel shows 0 instead of 'No data'.\nMeaning: nodes Kubernetes reports as not Ready or Unknown. Red when above zero.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 4,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "count(kube_node_status_condition{condition=\"Ready\",status=~\"false|unknown\"} == 1) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "Not ready",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "node_exporter targets down",
      "description": "Metric: `up` (Prometheus' own scrape result), job `orka-nodes`.\nPromQL: `count(up{job=\"orka-nodes\"} == 0) or vector(0)`.\nMeaning: node exporters this Prometheus cannot scrape. Distinct from Kubernetes readiness: a node can be Ready while its exporter is unreachable, and the reverse.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "count(up{job=\"orka-nodes\"} == 0) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "Down",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Nodes not Ready (detail)",
      "description": "Metric: `kube_node_status_condition`, job `kube-state-metrics`, `condition=\"Ready\"`, `status!=\"true\"`, value 1. Instant query shown as a table (columns: node, status). Empty table = every node Ready.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "kube_node_status_condition{condition=\"Ready\",status!=\"true\"} == 1",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "format": "table"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      },
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true,
              "Value": true,
              "__name__": true,
              "job": true,
              "instance": true,
              "endpoint": true,
              "service": true,
              "namespace": true,
              "pod": true,
              "uid": true,
              "cluster": true,
