        "content": "These parts of the Customer X asks have **no metric** at any endpoint documented as customer-reachable. They are shown so the dashboard does not imply coverage it does not have.\n\n| Ask | What would be needed | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| D3 / D1 | VM disk **allocated vs physical** (over-commit) | no metric; only host free space exists |\n| D2 | Image-cache size, cached-image count, stale entries | no metric |\n| R1 | Orka Engine / agent / WindowServer process health; virtual-kubelet heartbeat | virtual-kubelet exposes no `/metrics`; no Engine or agent metric listed |\n| R2 | Per-VM health or liveness; per-VM, per-node or per-namespace breakdown | operator metrics are 10 unlabelled series (the `vm_namespace` label is a 3.7.0-alpha addition) |\n| O3 | Firewall throughput, discards, session counts | not on the cluster; reached only via the MacStadium portal GraphQL API |\n| O2 | Notification by MacStadium | not a metric; internal alerting exists but customer notification is undocumented |\n\nAlerting itself (an alert at 80% disk, for example) would be a Prometheus alert rule plus Alertmanager on the customer's side. This dashboard only draws thresholds; it does not send alerts."
